  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r\rLocation Plan \rSite Plan\rProposed Site Plan\rProposed Shopfront - 916-PL-105 Rev. 03\rFootfall Report - Merkur Slots\rPlanning Brochure - Merkur Slots\rNoise Assessment\rHeritage Statement\rSecured by Design Measures\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Prior to the opening of the adult gaming centre, the reinstatement of the railings shall be fully completed in accordance with the approved details.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance and preserve the character of the Conservation Area.\r",
    "The external finishing materials shall match those indicated on the Approved Plans and Application Form.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 (as amended) 1 September 2020, or any amending Order, the premises shall only be used as an Adult Gaming Centre and shall not be used for any other purpose besides the granted sui generis Use Class, or for any other purpose without the express written permission of the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: In the interest of ensuring the effective control of the premises for the uses applied.\r",
    "The use of amplified music on the premises is prohibited at all times.\r\rReason: To ensure that the use of the premises does not prejudice the amenities of the occupiers of nearby residential properties.\r"
  ],
